Alembic migrations for the LlmForge PostgreSQL database.

From `backend/`, set `DATABASE_URL` for the intended database and run
`python -m alembic upgrade head` before starting a new backend image.
`alembic/env.py` reads the URL from the environment (or `backend/.env`) and
converts `postgresql://` URLs for the asyncpg driver. CI runs these migrations
only against its disposable PostgreSQL service, not the hosted database.

Review historical migrations before upgrading a database with existing data:
revision `i2j3k4l5m6n7` intentionally truncates legacy benchmark tables as
part of the workspace reset. Back up data you intend to keep.
